## Your move
You are in the **Trader** stance, docked at sol_station. The task this turn is a fixed reading: fan out `orient()`, `prices()` and `missions()` as one concurrent batch, then note one line with your credits, the item carrying the highest `best_buy`, and how many missions are on the board, and return the prices Outcome. Before writing it I checked the three gotchas it trips over.

1. **Concurrent, not sequential** — one `await Promise.all([orient(), prices(), missions()])`, exactly the three calls, no work between them.
2. **`prices()` is not awaited-in-isolation** — every play function returns `Promise<Outcome>`; I take the array and read `detail.quotes`.
3. **Highest `best_buy` from the real quote shape** — a quote is `{item_id, best_buy, best_buy_qty, best_sell, best_sell_qty, spread, held, stored}`. I pick `best.quotes[0].best_buy` among rows whose `best_buy > 0` (a zero/negative value is "not buyable here"), and name the item's `item_id` in the note. I read `credits` from `orient().now?.credits`. Mission count comes from `missions().detail` (the board) — I count its `missions`/`active` array when present, else fall back to a stated "unparsed" so the note never shows `undefined`. The final `return` is the prices Outcome, as the task asks.

```ts
import {orient, prices, missions, note, type Outcome} from 'play';

export default async function main() {
  // One batch: all three reads fan out together, not one after another.
  const [o, p, m] = await Promise.all([orient(), prices(), missions()]);

  const credits = o.now?.credits ?? 0;

  // The item with the highest best_buy at this counter (skip rows that do not buy at all).
  const quotes = p.detail?.quotes ?? [];
  const best = quotes.reduce<{item_id: string; best_buy: number} | null>(
    (top, q) => (q.best_buy > 0 && (top === null || q.best_buy > top.best_buy)
      ? {item_id: q.item_id, best_buy: q.best_buy}
      : top),
    null
  );

  // How many missions are on the board.
  const d: any = m.detail ?? {};
  const list = Array.isArray(d.missions) ? d.missions
    : Array.isArray(d.active) ? d.active
    : Array.isArray(d.listed) ? d.listed
    : Array.isArray(d.available) ? d.available
    : null;
  const missionCount = list ? list.length : null;
  const missionText = missionCount === null
    ? `${m.status} (${m.why ?? 'board not parsed'})`
    : `${missionCount} mission(s)`;

  note(`credits ${credits} · top best_buy ${best ? best.best_buy : 0} on ${best?.item_id ?? '(nothing buyable here)'} · ${missionText} on the board`);

  return p; // the prices Outcome, as the task asks
}
